#{[{:activity/_scope [{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120684} :activity/id #uuid "72f4cece-c3b1-5eb9-88d1-e1d563f3b9f1" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120684 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186121039 :tutorial/content "The **null space** of a matrix $A$ is the set of all the solutions of the equation $A\\mathbf{x}= \\mathbf{0},$ and is denoted by $\\textrm{Null}(A).$ \n\nTo illustrate, let's consider the following matrix:\n\n![](images/c3/c3bf583e98daad3fa753880b96c6ba85bce697f3434690977c5679b64ffd4882.svg)\n\nThe null space consists of all the solutions of $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}.$ For example, the vectors ![](images/9d/9d94e47625ee3c9d6fdff788db07e925ec2375e6c57cc6c1d8897ba423749abf.svg) ![](images/e5/e5a5f6b93eccdf25da72ea39af64a4a5cca7b0a03d5f469cb85554dc6dc12f88.svg) and $\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ all satisfy the equation $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0},$ so they are all elements of the null space:\n\n![](images/5e/5ededa27ee77302b18683f91e37d854a68cd3ba6ceacc7e2a6068a2730b4a9bf.svg)" :tutorial/id #uuid "3d284a1f-e3a9-5b48-97e4-d621a81b5237" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3204 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "4c3bb184-f74c-5977-a8e6-98bdcb8a2dd8" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120685}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120685 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119812 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3c3466c-dfb0-5b5f-b556-ce57a1d78519"} :step/id #uuid "8a689cc9-53dd-54fa-a611-9d759b6620a8" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120686}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120686 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119813 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9171c6fb-ad0b-538f-b982-a2502a20e253"} :step/id #uuid "99922077-a3d5-5752-963a-c25d4e87ccf4" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120751}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120687 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "465ce2b7-352e-5050-a5e4-0753fbacebf5"} :step/id #uuid "5062db3d-b1a3-544d-a0cd-7dd7a74b40af"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120751 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186121063 :tutorial/content "Let's again consider the following matrix:\n\n![](images/8f/8fa69630c71d5106ed04a5281681992687174891b1c0978521c12e914cb3a0b0.svg)\n\nTo find an expression for the null space using set-builder notation, we need to find all the solutions of $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Let's start by considering the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\, \\mathbf{0}]$ and finding its reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,0] & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st column). The second column is not a pivot column.\n\nNow, we convert the reduced matrix back into a system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ 0 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nHere, $\\color{blue}x_1$ is a basic variable (it corresponds to the pivot column), while $\\color{red}x_2$ is a free variable (it corresponds to the non-pivot column). Because there is a free variable, the system $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}$ has infinitely many solutions. \n\nFrom the first equation we get ${\\color{blue}x_1}=-3{\\color{red}x_2},$ so the set of all the solutions of $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}$ is\n![](images/8c/8c5541adb07cb58136d71fb4e3218981f1717b929f22acbe55d133cd0c395870.svg)\n\n**Note:** It is not necessary to consider the full augmented matrix $[A \\,|\\, \\mathbf{0}]$ since the last column won't be changed during the process of reduction. Really, we just need to find the reduced row echelon form of the matrix $A$ and then set up the corresponding system." :tutorial/id #uuid "895e6e15-cec9-50e1-9bed-dff731650d72" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3943 :tutorial/title "Writing the Null Space using Set-Builder Notation"} :step/id #uuid "7af33686-5798-591e-a725-45ae0719e381" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120687}}] :activity/title "The Null Space of a Matrix" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186120048} {:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436469} :activity/id #uuid "f955c261-e47c-561a-aad8-66424916ac00" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436468 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436465 :question/id #uuid "0f9d6921-1029-58c3-84e2-79c33a9e57b1"} :step/id #uuid "15381825-f698-53f0-84f0-2e86406279e2" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436470}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436469 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317454 :question/id #uuid "870e5cfd-95f3-5e52-b251-41fd48145e5a"} :step/id #uuid "29910b71-b3db-5759-85dc-176a6617f370" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436472}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436470 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247206 :question/id #uuid "91993936-f250-5744-8e70-dfa072854477"} :step/id #uuid "3e7e9496-7cc4-53b7-8c6c-41b5bec20173" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436471}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436471 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436466 :question/id #uuid "312e3366-ac87-55a7-a43b-4cbe0aecef1d"} :step/id #uuid "b0354757-cd1b-5c5a-beab-edd97603bc08"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436472 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436467 :question/id #uuid "b6c9ad88-847a-5bc3-8131-a821e5ea8f1f"} :step/id #uuid "d5566fb1-8f87-5400-942c-97c4b723a589" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436468}}] :activity/title "The Null Space of a Matrix" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436446}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186048181 :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119812 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119623 :question/id #uuid "fe2f3934-fa5c-5a59-be7e-00b6e4889063" :question/math-academy-id "e-4810" :question/problem "The matrix $A$ and vectors $\\mathbf{b}_1$, $\\mathbf{b}_2$, $\\mathbf{b}_3$ are given below. Which of the vectors lie in $\\textrm{Null}(A)?$\n\n![](images/53/53e17b54ff077d45401bdc4754ccdcff5d0cad20e8d5b477b7a9e0aec37ab52c.svg)" :question/worked-solution "A vector $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Null}(A)$ if $A\\mathbf{b}=\\mathbf{0}.$ So, we need to compute the product of $A$ and each of the given vectors and check whether it is equal to $\\mathbf{0}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{b}_{1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -6 \\\\ -5 & 10 \\\\ -8 & 16\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-27 \\\\ 45 \\\\ 72\\end{bmatrix}\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -6 \\\\ -5 & 10 \\\\ -8 & 16\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=0\\,✓ \\\\ A{b}_{3} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -6 \\\\ -5 & 10 \\\\ -8 & 16\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-15 \\\\ 25 \\\\ 40\\end{bmatrix}\\ne 0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $\\mathbf{b}_2$ lies in $\\textrm{Null}(A).$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3c3466c-dfb0-5b5f-b556-ce57a1d78519" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120323 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f5635325-a935-5bda-8f6a-48de48a325d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$b_{1}$ and $b_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118078} {:answer/id #uuid "159b3301-30f8-5c8f-8483-f0f44c83e4c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$b_{1}$ and $b_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118079} {:answer/id #uuid "2eb7ac93-77f6-52d6-8984-45b733231ff9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118080} {:answer/id #uuid "33cfb83f-fad5-53c9-a109-3bd929049adc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$b_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118081} {:answer/id #uuid "64276734-b93f-595f-9b85-e7c498de8052" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$b_{2}$ and $b_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118082}] :answer-field/id #uuid "3c89b1dd-b792-59c4-85f5-7826a5f40ab3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118077}] :question/id #uuid "35fc1454-840e-5c03-95ff-3b12eaf185e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-34331" :question/problem "The matrix $A$ and vectors $b_{1}$, $b_{2}$, $b_{3}$ are given below. Which of the vectors lie in $Null(A)$?\n\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}, b_{1} = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}, b_{2} = \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}, b_{3} = \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120334 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81cb86eb-45d4-554e-8250-65ce8076104d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$b_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118134} {:answer/id #uuid "035229a8-13a9-5621-95fb-c1315bb978ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$b_{1}$ and $b_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118135} {:answer/id #uuid "2527d318-646e-5d4f-903c-6cfb27c41b3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$b_{2}$ and $b_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118136} {:answer/id #uuid "5f42020e-426e-53bd-a97f-a507d368163d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118137} {:answer/id #uuid "714af33f-56f1-50b0-a345-d5ab9c4f703f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$b_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118138}] :answer-field/id #uuid "07456100-88a2-5ca9-8116-0d0d4891f2cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118133}] :question/id #uuid "44f2c49f-d9d7-5739-960b-cb53b5e61745" :question/math-academy-id "q-34390" :question/problem "The matrix $A$ and vectors $b_{1}$, $b_{2}$, $b_{3}$ are given below. Which of the vectors lie in $Null(A)$?\n\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}, b_{1} = \\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}, b_{2} = \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}, b_{3} = \\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247201 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "248916b2-451f-5a2e-b997-50d411bf2840" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244638} {:answer/id #uuid "7a77e598-9518-5998-99b7-e7ee00caabc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{2}$ and ${b}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245391} {:answer/id #uuid "7c53eb8a-85a9-53a9-9264-04831b2db7a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245403} {:answer/id #uuid "8394708e-1cf9-586c-88f3-d1695c1f771e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245470} {:answer/id #uuid "c0a4be47-4c7f-5a58-8db6-e87fe061f0f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246033}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245403} :answer-field/id #uuid "a181ae41-10e4-54c0-8ae6-f1bff44fe7d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246831}] :question/id #uuid "1fc4bebd-83f9-51c8-a49f-5447951d22bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-111079" :question/problem "The matrix $A$ and vectors ${b}_{1}$, ${b}_{2}$, ${b}_{3}$ are given below. Which of the vectors lie in $\\text{Null}(A)?$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Null}(A)$ if $Ab=0.$ So, we need to compute the product of $A$ and each of the given vectors and check whether it is equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{b}_{1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=0\\,✓ \\\\ A{b}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -15\\end{bmatrix}\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{3} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{3}$ lie in $\\text{Null}(A).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247205 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ec9fb62-b74e-5f73-a9d7-24cdd8241f08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244733} {:answer/id #uuid "40c874be-9d6a-5355-9a2d-1de28e66c7fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244881} {:answer/id #uuid "4c0cb95e-5081-5fb0-b7e4-fccdc6b1560f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244990} {:answer/id #uuid "6477b993-602e-50ef-a5bf-f697d4de187f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245198} {:answer/id #uuid "d96b8ef7-018c-5dcb-aebd-a4407210a617" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246246}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245198} :answer-field/id #uuid "201f345b-15d4-533c-a4c9-80d020de8ac0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246600}] :question/id #uuid "6241d446-37e4-5ee6-bee7-f843f3fd7347" :question/math-academy-id "q-111091" :question/problem "The matrix $A$ and vectors ${b}_{1}$, ${b}_{2}$, ${b}_{3}$ are given below. Which of the vectors lie in $\\text{Null}(A)?$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Null}(A)$ if $Ab=0.$ So, we need to compute the product of $A$ and each of the given vectors and check whether it is equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{b}_{1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}39 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}34 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{3} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-33 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}\\ne 0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, none of the vectors lies in $\\text{Null}(A).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317441 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3de74079-f3cf-5def-aa1f-da3bc1be2fc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315476} {:answer/id #uuid "635f68a6-04d1-59e7-961c-48cb02bb94b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315676} {:answer/id #uuid "8118e81d-84eb-5f5d-8914-ed2e08788b0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315829} {:answer/id #uuid "dc334c09-7d2c-58fc-8e10-b27547ac5d85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316344} {:answer/id #uuid "f23e33d1-49d6-51b0-8d86-dbaead63b9d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316468}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315676} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe0284c0-67f8-5e76-ad83-63edd1004483" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317152}] :question/id #uuid "0d4cb2fe-d794-5b24-afd6-08f39ce18357" :question/math-academy-id "q-34384" :question/problem "The matrix $A$ and vectors ${b}_{1}$, ${b}_{2}$, ${b}_{3}$ are given below. Which of the vectors lie in $\\text{Null}(A)?$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & -10 \\\\ 9 & 15\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Null}(A)$ if $Ab=0.$ So, we need to compute the product of $A$ and each of the given vectors and check whether it is equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{b}_{1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & -10 \\\\ 9 & 15\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 90\\end{bmatrix}\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & -10 \\\\ 9 & 15\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-59 \\\\ 118 \\\\ -33\\end{bmatrix}\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{3} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & -10 \\\\ 9 & 15\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 180\\end{bmatrix}\\ne 0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, none of the vector lies in $\\text{Null}(A).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402362 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0957d54-3a75-5c9c-85ed-c3fc9e27319a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402364} {:answer/id #uuid "a07d906a-9817-56bc-a8bc-f84fb817ea22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ only" :db/id #e