ligned}A-(-1)I & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-(-1)I)x=0$ gives us the eigenverctor ${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{3}=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-I)x=0$ gives us the eigenverctor ${v}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n**Step 3.** We construct the diagonal matrix $D$ and the invertible matrix $P$ in the usual way, and this gives us the following:\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,P=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402575 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99584719-3306-525f-8ff1-816884430043" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$D=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and $P=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402577} {:answer/id #uuid "91430aee-305c-5083-a738-7954753b326b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$D=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$ and $P=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402578} {:answer/id #uuid "2955626a-1299-50b8-8b43-a19bf6c7b887" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$D=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and $P=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402579} {:answer/id #uuid "34185d7e-94a1-519b-9e07-ed69ef1852ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$D=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}