n the usual way:\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}-6x \\\\ 9x+5y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe require a $2\\times 2$ matrix $T$ such that\n    \n\n$$\nT\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-6x \\\\ 9x+5y\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNotice that\n    \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-6x \\\\ 9x+5y\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n    Therefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n    \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344997 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04aa5497-f840-54f8-98f0-be027f861809" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342288} {:answer/id #uuid "202b3099-18e9-568e-9c8e-0a7b898a184c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342503} {:answer/id #uuid "802e0ac5-506d-5dd2-8a4c-773415166bf5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343338} {:answer/id #uuid "bfa950f0-5b53-5331-aa39-5720d9906885" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343919} {:answer/id #uuid "cc5391c8-1495-55ed-8015-9475520ea3a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344036}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343919} :answer-field/id #uuid "aaaad83c-801e-5126-977a-c5d65ee130c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344791}] :question/id #uuid "7d2d84a3-965c-5e39-bd49-b19a736f3967" :question/math-academy-id "q-74941" :question/problem "Find the standard matrix that represents  the  linear  transformation $T$, where\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}3y+x \\\\ y-x\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, rewrite the order of the variables in the usual way:\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x+3y \\\\ -x+y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe require a $2\\times 2$ matrix $T$ such that\n    \n\n$$\nT\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}x+3y \\\\ -x+y\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNotice that\n    \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}x+3y \\\\ -x+y\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n    \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344998 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fc3172c-d72c-56b7-9f41-3386f52ea7a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342637} {:answer/id #uuid "31367fc5-0608-5275-a124-56a2a0a7aa62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342651} {:answer/id #uuid "9d84155b-c31e-568c-a731-fed5a32f974f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343623} {:answer/id #uuid "a389204d-43e1-5d5e-9ae1-114697e733cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343676} {:answer/id #uuid "d6e1bced-90f1-5f08-a09d-b857f821bbbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344124}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344124} :answer-field/id #uuid "08424f00-0cd2-55a3-8b49-3a4fc5638f65" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344509}] :question/id #uuid "27919ecd-01db-59d6-ba61-57dce5d88f97" :question/math-academy-id "q-74943" :question/problem "Find the standard matrix that represents  the  linear  transformation $T$, where\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}-5y \\\\ 2y+x\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, rewrite the order of the variables in the usual way:\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}-5y \\\\ x+2y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe require a $2\\times 2$ matrix $T$ such that\n    \n\n$$\nT\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5y \\\\ x+2y\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNotice that\n    \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5y \\\\ x+2y\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n    \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344999 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "196a6c86-d084-51ad-a8b9-73914baaba88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342459} {:answer/id #uuid "607e457d-034f-5ac3-ae34-66f83d96ffee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343057} {:answer/id #uuid "9e19ba11-5d98-582a-b307-cc2b06f0c8fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343629} {:answer/id #uuid "c9c901cc-8ad2-543a-9296-8187bc2849dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344010} {:answer/id #uuid "ef888896-0dbe-5d39-8c9b-b4f4f5a1f75e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344343}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342459} :answer-field/id #uuid "0123ba14-cda9-50e8-b776-935fb8e44944" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344496}] :question/id #uuid "584e2c14-f34a-5c2c-b72f-ebdc1add2440" :question/math-academy-id "q-74944" :question/problem "Find the standard matrix that represents  the  linear  transformation $T$, where\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}2y-5z+x \\\\ z-y+3x \\\\ -z-2x+3y\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, rewrite the order of the variables in the usual way:\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x+2y-5z \\\\ 3x-y+z \\\\ -2x+3y-z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe require a $3\\times 3$ matrix $T$ such that\n\n$$\nT\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}x+2y-5z \\\\ 3x-y+z \\\\ -2x+3y-z\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}x+2y-5z \\\\ 3x-y+z \\\\ -2x+3y-z\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351475 :question/answer-fie