.\n$$\n\nNotice that\n    \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-12 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-12x+5y \\\\ x+3y\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n    Therefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n    \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-12 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation With Rearranging"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124514 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124323 :question/id #uuid "77bd52ee-454e-5794-83e5-991e7e4c13b5" :question/math-academy-id "e-5433" :question/problem "What is the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ whose standard matrix is ![](images/4a/4a4616061123e27093fa73d17de5c81fb68527b83993cba4eec22fc0368fe364.png)" :question/worked-solution "Consider a general vector ![](images/c5/c5e95c3c6c86e0719be77fc3db865c7a81995ef386ce7508ccef19ab307a783a.png) Multiplying by the matrix $T,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}8x-y \\\\ -5x-2y\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $\\,\\mathbf{T}\\,$ is given by\n\n![](images/e6/e6c0ddd895406c6b79e4c520a7a4002060c917b51a6070f134be8c47dd63de0b.png)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "656da168-af12-53c2-8add-2c82cf71b31c" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125113 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97a0fc1e-4d60-51bd-9431-a359d024fa33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T: \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}-2y + 4z \\\\ 2x - 3y \\\\ x - y + z\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123279} {:answer/id #uuid "a162e196-cb33-54a2-a2bb-b55d299f7027" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T: \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}2