answer/id #uuid "4b6a9d05-6e01-51ba-86f0-6786a3d3f6e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\times 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300351} {:answer/id #uuid "67ffd28f-e55a-506b-96fc-0977cb9caa42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\times 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300485} {:answer/id #uuid "834c1c57-436e-55e7-93e9-e88179c019c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\times 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300615} {:answer/id #uuid "87024881-b24a-5f18-93b5-f70758bfee2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\times 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300640} {:answer/id #uuid "c32ed394-a262-572d-b62f-17195041b680" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\times 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300938}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\times 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300938} :answer-field/id #uuid "66daf1ee-811c-53d2-b782-685fe297c127" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301551}] :question/id #uuid "9c49211b-ae4b-51fe-8084-ee8c6ceee565" :question/math-academy-id "q-32173" :question/problem "A partitioned matrix $M$ contains the following blocks: \n\n- ${M}_{12},$ which is a $2\\times 1$ block\n\n- ${M}_{21},$ which is a $2\\times 3$ block\n\n- ${M}_{22},$ which is a $2\\times 1$ block\n\nWhat are the dimensions of ${M}_{11}?$" :question/worked-solution "We have a matrix of the form\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}{M}_{11} & {M}_{12} \\\\ {M}_{21} & {M}_{22}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}?\\times ? & 2\\times 1 \\\\ 2\\times 3 & 2\\times 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${M}_{11}$ must be a $2\\times 3$ block."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326930 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06430929-d890-59e2-be77-7b85c0609cac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\times 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324030} {:answer/id #uuid "5c47551f-20c5-590d-a8d1-f1cd82d705e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\times 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324736} {:answer/id #uuid "95218ee8-17a1-591d-9ef4-574032f69a03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\times 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325240} {:answer/id #uuid "964459fc-6abb-5842-a536-26695b7207e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\times 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325252} {:answer/id #uuid "da6ece0b-8d76-51bd-b26d-075326edfc3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\times 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325874}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\times 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325240} :answer-field/id #uuid "019a542b-7623-532e-b323-23b29bcbc733" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326222}] :question/id #uuid "3b9e0d32-b5dc-57e1-95b6-1cc48988ca5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-42123" :question/problem "A partitioned matrix $M$ contains the following blocks: \n\n- ${M}_{11},$ which is a $2\\times 3$ block\n\n- ${M}_{12},$ which is a $2\\times 2$ block\n\n- ${M}_{22},$ which is a $1\\times 2$ block\n\nWhat are the dimensions of ${M}_{21}?$" :question/worked-solution "We have a matrix of the form\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}{M}_{11} & {M}_{12} \\\\ {M}_{21} & {M}_{22}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2\\times 3 & 2\\times 2 \\\\ ?\\times ? & 1\\times 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${M}_{21}$ must be a $1\\times 3$ block."}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Dimensions of Blocks in Partitioned Matrices"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115334 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115151 :question/id #uuid "6fe1d3e1-27a7-5e9d-9776-d66c19dae753" :question/math-academy-id "e-9094" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are block diagonal?\n\n![](images/a6/a610512000d95e3ed80559431e25501a9d498d342e7c180864720bbeb2ee10d4.png)" :question/worked-solution "A block diagonal matrix can be partitioned so that it has only square blocks on the main diagonal, and all the other blocks contain only zeros.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $A$ is a block diagonal matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n![](images/f6/f6e977aff21319bb8e0cbb251d36577966f84060e809e3485f9019e85cd3538e.png)\n\n- $B$ is *not* a block diagonal matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above:\n![](images/59/597e27b2f470bc60717eb3341d2f3e87f411c0a4c796a58ee3aa83c691971517.png)\n\n- $C$ is *not* a block diagonal matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A$ only.\""} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf19e2ee-7c42-58b0-9254-5a44f315288a" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115833 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3f82a1a-0910-5204-ade6-b09516beebaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113936} {:answer/id #uuid "b7cabae1-3537-551f-bacb-eeb257da92db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113937} {:answer/id #uuid "f1445472-cf42-5137-9a4c-33f1846df997" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113938} {:answer/id #uuid "6d2b2940-0c1b-5519-9f2c-2b1346efcf8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113939} {:answer/id #uuid "6d491115-ea7d-5cf8-9f72-0bff8adf58bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113940}] :answer-field/id #uuid "07895415-100a-55bc-b24c-ef261744b6a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113935}] :question/id #uuid "1be5bafb-5e31-52b5-aa3b-bae9966d6b24" :question/math-academy-id "q-42132" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are block upper triangular?\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}, B = \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}, C = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115834 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17aa9c3c-1177-5ab6-9436-4ed101b94dc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459963} {:answer/id #uuid "37e030ed-add9-5c5c-b9c2-a9b03bda4a42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459964}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459963} :answer-field/id #uuid "575277b5-4a90-527e-97ae-d9ef4882fdfa" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460848} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3757cf46-44d8-5925-81e3-501b153e88c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459965} {:answer/id #uuid "9e164199-e408-5a69-9bc2-cd5d71bdf400" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459966}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459965} :answer-field/id #uuid "053227d5-2248-514c-83ab-a486205fe2d4" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460849} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "921e04de-799e-5beb-ab08-d9814cdcfb37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459967} {:answer/id #uuid "7574341a-6c1f-5a8e-961a-b129941c9412" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459968}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459968} :answer-field/id #uuid "9efeee9c-63b6-5691-bb36-c331fd5f912d" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460850}] :question/id #uuid "12fdac9a-07ca-546f-8c67-8327e7b0318b" :question/math-academy-id "q-42134" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are block diagonal?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A block diagonal matrix can be partitioned so that it has only square blocks on the main diagonal, and all the other blocks contain only zeros.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $A$ is *not* a block diagonal matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $B$ is *not* a block diagonal matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $C$ is a block diagonal matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$C$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266090 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c3c38d0-c5ee-51a5-a634-73869c8a9051" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463988} {:answer/id #uuid "a5abb1b5-aa47-59c8-bb04-5bab40e3a464" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463989}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463988} :answer-field/id #uuid "260a60c0-4a86-55b9-b153-b9972312fe23" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464928} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e9349efc-83ce-557d-a5dd-eaaf0f4b374f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463990} {:answer/id #uuid "500eb1d4-4cd3-5a05-9f47-b1ee5ab4aad4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463991}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463990} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4f7105d-60c5-5892-a339-4d601a308a96" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464929} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9be3fd1e-0669-5f34-b527-da1a9b508b28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463992} {:answer/id #uuid "903ff4ef-beaf-5981-9576-02f1ee9ebc05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463993}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463992} :answer-field/id #uuid "9473659a-cb3e-51ed-8227-bcaa2678cdef" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464930}] :question/id #uuid "675c49ee-f80c-5132-87b4-3f13525060ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-131460" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are block diagonal?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A block diagonal matrix can be partitioned so that it has only square blocks on the main diagonal, and all the other blocks contain only zeros.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $A$ is *not* a block diagonal matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $B$ is *not* a block diagonal matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $C$ is *not* a block diagonal matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302081 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "635db59e-1cbe-5374-93a1-dc5600b113ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465963} {:answer/id #uuid "1380955a-7891-5ebb-8e6f-0ecb7cd8d163" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465964}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465963} :answer-field/id #uuid "747147b5-6f28-516b-9fbd-ed2b6847683b" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466825} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c00b5b07-5075-5047-bce9-30f2f0b43b4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465965} {:answer/id #uuid "1f347499-a2ef-5193-98a9-edc223ccddfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465966}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465965} :answer-field/id #uuid "dfb25ace-1008-524c-8fa4-94dc70d5efd6" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466826} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e08924d1-95b8-535a-aad8-72b551226515" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465967} {:answer/id #uuid "fd4d68b6-0db1-5d6f-8a30-e9cbd4a836ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465968}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465968} :answer-field/id #uuid "09f84aee-b132-58fa-9a7b-d7984b11fcb4" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466827}] :question/id #uuid "587dcbe8-780f-5ae0-a952-bc8f4458a90a" :question/math-academy-id "q-32176" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are block diagonal?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A block diagonal matrix can be partitioned so that it has only square blocks on the main diagonal, and all the other blocks contain only zeros.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $A$ is *not* a block diagonal matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $B$ is *not* a block diagonal matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $C$ is a block diagonal matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$C$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302082 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e074fd44-241e-5354-ac55-574c46320793" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465969} {:answer/id #uuid "c9f83324-3e40-5b90-bd0e-d0bb28e72fa8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465970}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465970} :answer-field/id #uuid "43fc67a8-d442-5472-ade2-018a534151c1" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466828} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66c40a5d-dc92-519c-8c9b-36cc0d76a52c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465971} {:answer/id #uuid "7d9eb1fa-cf44-5e53-8e6c-d71c41e60033" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465972}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465971} :answer-field/id #uuid "33e39b3f-5c6b-5047-bec7-489e6b7713bf" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466829} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d989e3c-b2a7-53a2-84f7-ed72a3c7274b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465973} {:answer/id #uuid "1919dfcb-4715-5a8a-b3ac-9c30fe778b71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465974}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465974} :answer-field/id #uuid "09f314cc-c8c7-5588-97e5-e9fdc6aa309a" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466830}] :question/id #uuid "1208e79a-a661-5205-bd4d-ce2da940348a" :question/math-academy-id "q-32177" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are block lower triangular?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 4 & 10\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A block lower triangular matrix can be partitioned so that it has only square blocks on the main diagonal, and the blocks above the main diagonal contain only zeros.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $A$ is a block lower triangular matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 4 & 10\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $B$ is *not* a block lower triangular matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $C$ is a block lower triangular matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A$ and $C$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326931 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "195c361c-f98a-56bc-95a9-a24d6ae95142" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467494} {:answer/id #uuid "087e2b8e-167a-55dd-a33c-443fc10c0a77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467495}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467495} :answer-field/id #uuid "3bcb8c2f-2a00-55cd-bda8-3dffe1628a2f" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468468} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "010a0770-3fce-59e2-86e4-c29d912931fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467496} {:answer/id #uuid "7127439e-6346-576e-adcf-02d5a6d602d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467497}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467497} :answer-field/id #uuid "e04e0008-7373-571f-9da6-ce0524c094b7" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468469} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33c9ca18-0830-5bb9-94a9-9ae66555b1a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467498} {:answer/id #uuid "095d4e7f-7b52-523f-ae5b-6a414007ba1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467499}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467498} :answer-field/id #uuid "82277b7d-af0a-5d41-83d1-80cb091465ec" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468470}] :question/id #uuid "366fb16a-48e3-5635-add3-b8c862272224" :question/math-academy-id "q-42127" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are block lower triangular?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A block lower triangular matrix can be partitioned so that it has only square blocks on the main diagonal, and the blocks above the main diagonal contain only zeros.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $A$ is a block lower triangular matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $B$ is a block lower triangular matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $C$ is *not* a block lower triangular matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A$ and $B$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329633 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf81b5d0-b61e-5203-bb54-801438d3461d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467500} {:answer/id #uuid "fd171565-81f8-50d3-8a91-05948557c95c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467501}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467500} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a853d7c-2687-518d-a446-c138652f4c7e" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468471} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc4d0664-5482-5544-9e91-690f058f2d43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467502} {:answer/id #uuid "12bbe01a-fe98-5ec1-a6c8-24a6cbbe1cca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467503}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467502} :answer-field/id #uuid "34b3dc6c-709b-5dee-acff-ac14c1ddc707" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468472} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "825129c8-74ee-54bf-8b70-10f615c4071d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467504} {:answer/id #uuid "35dfa222-4364-5bbd-af7c-c6cfea240e47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467505}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467504} :answer-field/id #uuid "5535032e-f5c6-5f9b-b4e5-bbd70b524e51" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468473}] :question/id #uuid "b1e9c127-3ff2-5d29-89f3-9a02b595895a" :question/math-academy-id "q-42138" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are block upper triangular?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A block upper triangular matrix can be partitioned so that it has only square blocks on the main diagonal, and the blocks below the main diagonal contain only zeros.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $A$ is *not* a block upper triangular matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix},\\,A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix},\\,A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $B$ is *not* a block upper triangular matrix since it can't be partitioned in a way described above:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $C$ is *not* a block upper triangular matrix since it can't be partitioned in a way described above:\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366945 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ead9eb7-6179-5dd3-bb4d-a0b6266823fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468870} {:answer/id #uuid "8b9840e8-0b71-5152-86ba-99ddfd860c5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468870} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea3fe40b-78a5-502f-88f4-ea17a1a7eed1" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470047} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63f648f4-6b6b-54ca-b233-6007032093f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468872} {:answer/id #uuid "3b188c3a-165e-5a4d-8e93-a4c74af56e13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468872} :answer-field/id #uuid "bac8d59a-f4f8-59b0-a422-e8fcb6fc24d7" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470048} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5d9824e-7b54-553e-bf8d-b4f60f9d4401" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468874} {:answer/id #uuid "ad3e8787-8c89-5c14-83be-c185f11748cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468875}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468875} :answer-field/id #uuid "3202f73f-6a44-5bd9-9c2c-4f8276a03317" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470049}] :question/id #uuid "3da29d09-2c10-59b3-aafb-a3f2d64ea706" :question/math-academy-id "q-109246" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are block upper triangular?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 9 & -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A block upper triangular matrix can be partitioned so that it has only square blocks on the main diagonal, and the blocks below the main diagonal contain only zeros.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $A$is *not* a block upper triangular matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 9 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $B$ is *not* a block upper triangular matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $C$ is a block upper triangular matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$C$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367387 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7308f1e2-e007-5c2e-907c-22bc98d0f77f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468936} {:answer/id #uuid "0a28f853-0fa0-505b-b5dc-dabd085a65de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468937}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468937} :answer-field/id #uuid "e40a305a-51fa-577b-b0d1-2f30645cf2f2" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470080} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf2571f9-f77c-5433-917a-edf1ee3295de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468938} {:answer/id #uuid "7347e1c9-bf88-5d63-9f71-a549b59a6be4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468939}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468938} :answer-field/id #uuid "36b3f1bf-b723-5f6b-b4f8-d6df672c4826" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470081} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a528447-3459-57b5-88c5-a12c03f95ffe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468940} {:answer/id #uuid "23b0245a-f580-5cdc-a3a0-64c481c6bc0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468941}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468941} :answer-field/id #uuid "af9bae30-f4e2-59ef-9906-b389016cca44" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470082}] :question/id #uuid "ba25631a-3eab-56f2-a3d7-d0c6da834d90" :question/math-academy-id "q-131447" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are block diagonal?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A block diagonal matrix can be partitioned so that it has only square blocks on the main diagonal, and all the other blocks contain only zeros.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $A$ is a block diagonal matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $B$ is *not* a block diagonal matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $C$ is a block diagonal matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A$ and $C$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396613 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7e68721-1e8c-56a5-a25e-20d32a560654" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470853} {:answer/id #uuid "f3a535ba-5cfa-5970-a938-26f3c594993d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470854}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470854} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0257ee2-c864-5405-bc21-712dc76df852" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471932} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "775e5742-9972-51b8-b6af-ae4ade5ae9ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470855} {:answer/id #uuid "9443b334-1f11-553a-95cf-10edf7a52a76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470856}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470856} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ecf819d-ba3e-547e-9704-406e5e9b7d59" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471933} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e33e7564-1735-5427-9e70-60f44a0e5c0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470857} {:answer/id #uuid "29445738-cbab-570a-85ae-1651b69dc6d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470858}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470858} :answer-field/id #uuid "80cc35c3-1dad-5d2d-a2b0-facf839095ec" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471934}] :question/id #uuid "c07f2a41-0b84-51be-b671-ed8827d6cdfb" :question/math-academy-id "q-109247" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are block lower triangular?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 9\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A block lower triangular matrix can be partitioned so that it has only square blocks on the main diagonal, and the blocks above the main diagonal contain only zeros.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $A$ is a block lower triangular matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $B$ is a block lower triangular matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $C$ is a block lower triangular matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A,$ $B,$ and $C.$\""}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Block Diagonal and Block Triangular Matrices"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115335 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115152 :question/id #uuid "e0360a5e-97c7-5a9b-9d13-ba05360e4d78" :question/math-academy-id "e-9096" :question/problem "Find \n![](images/f9/f9f02df9d1e971ccea2d5abb67f95866bb334e636e5d39ec59d14a617d8f15f0.png)\ngiven that \n![](images/58/58f57ca9a1782c7edc2367b2aed9798e8e2c1eb8318000e6202b3fa0746c6a90.png)" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we have  a block upper triangular matrix. Therefore, its determinant is equal to the product of the determinants of the diagonal blocks:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & e & 4 \\\\ 0 & h & 8\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & e & 4 \\\\ 0 & h & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =7\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}e & 4 \\\\ h & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =7\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =42\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b507561-8134-50ff-8c23-c4ecc546450d" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id