" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367414}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367410} :answer-field/id #uuid "be6aa0ff-ec0d-58f5-b91b-35aaf2d39bab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367409}] :question/id #uuid "fcb154ec-04b4-53f4-bb0d-67f9c8aa5c85" :question/math-academy-id "q-131655" :question/problem "Find $\\,|\\begin{aligned}p & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & q & 5 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ r & 0 & 0 & \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}|$ given that $\\,|\\begin{aligned}p & 2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & q & 5 \\\\ 8 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|=12.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we have  a block lower triangular matrix. Therefore, its determinant is equal to the product of the diagonal blocks' determinants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}p & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & q & 5 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ r & 0 & 0 & \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}p & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & q & 5 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ r & 0 & 0 & \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}p & 2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & q & 5 \\\\ 8 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|\\cdot \\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & =12\\cdot \\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367971 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42cf5542-0289-5dec-a071-29770b99b3eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367973} {:answer/id #uuid "b0d368b0-3fe5-5821-a75b-cb36898eadc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367974} {:answer/id #uuid "1f3e4090-3023-5287-89a3-493d5d621214" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367975} {:answer/id #uuid "e2d8a4d5-ef76-50e4-a75e-2bf24eedd773" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367976} {:answer/id #uuid "f8eace11-55fe-5542-9c70-079f9177d0e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367977}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367975} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8b04c9b-a297-56c0-bc58-cb471f7a2a39" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367972}] :question/id #uuid "89791f16-1e44-5ecb-98bd-8a1b36242eee" :question/math-academy-id "q-32172" :question/problem "Find \n$|\\begin{aligned}-3 & b & 0 \\\\ d & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}|$\ngiven that \n$|\\begin{aligned}-3 & b \\\\ d & 2\\end{aligned}|=-7.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we have a block diagonal matrix. Therefore, its determinant is equal to the product of the diagonal blocks' determinants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-3 & b & 0 \\\\ d & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & b & 0 \\\\ d & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & b \\\\ d & 2\\end{aligned}|\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =(-7)\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =28.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Determinant of a Block Diagonal or Block Triangular Matrix"}] :topic/math-academy-id 1735 :topic/title "Partitioned and Block Matrices"}]}
